{title: A True Israelite}
{subtitle: John 1:45; 1:46; 1:47; 1:48–49; 21:1–2}
{key: D#m}
{tempo: 85}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [D#m] | [D#m] | [D#m] | [D#m] |
| [D#m] | [D#m] | [F#] | [C#] |
| [G#] [F#6] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D#m]Philip found Nathanael in the light
Told him of Je[F#]sus from Na[C#]zareth
[D#m]We found the one Moses wrote about
In [F#]the law and the prop[C#]hets
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[D#m]Can anything good come from there
Natha[F#]nael asked with a frown
[C#]Come and see said Philip
[G#]Then the journey began
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[D#m]See here is a true Israe[F#]lite
In whom there is no de[C#]ceit
No de[G#]ceit in his heart
A true Israe[D#m]lite
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Instrumental}
| [D#m] | [F#] | [C#] | [G#] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D#m]I saw you under the fig tree
[F#]Before Philip called you [C#]
[D#m]Nathanael asked how he knew
Jesus spoke the [F#]truth [C#]
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [D#m] | [F#] | [C#] | [G#] | ×3

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[D#m]Rabbi you are the Son of God
[F#]King of Israel is your name
The [C#]fig tree witness remains
[G#]Faith begins in the light
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[D#m]By the Sea of Tiberias
He re[F#]vealed himself again
[C#]Nathanael from Cana
[G#]Witness to the risen [D#m][F#][C#][G#]Lord
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
| [D#m] | [F#] | [C#] | [G#] |
| [D#m] | [D#m] |
